<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's short-term PHIBOR rates down.</title>
<headline>Manila's short-term PHIBOR rates down.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) slipped for one-week to one-month maturities, reflecting the easing of rates in the overnight market, traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>PHIBOR rates for two to six months, however, were slightly higher, while the one-year rate was steady.</p>
<p>&quot;The longer tenors are not as volatile. People do not easily change positions because of the longer time horizon,&quot;a foreign bank dealer said.</p>
<p>PHIBOR represents the rates at which banks are willing to swap their pesos for dollars.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  SEPT 19		 SEPT 18</p>
<p>    1 W		12  5/16		12  1/2</p>
<p>    2 W		12  1/4		 12  3/8</p>
<p>    1 M		12  3/16		12  5/16</p>
<p>    2 M		12			11 15/16</p>
<p>    3 M		11  7/8		 11 13/16</p>
<p>    6 M		11  7/8		 11 13/16</p>
<p>    12M		12			12</p>
<p>    VAL		20-Sep		  19-Sep</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom (632) 841-8937</p>
